From: FatBoy721 <203330788+FatBoy721@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:15:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: forward HDMI converter service requests on T6050

The J714s HDMI port is the same design as the T6030 one: dcpext drives an
on-board DP-to-HDMI converter whose HPD is a GPIO, and the DPTX core has no
HPD of its own (macOS: "connectTo ... supportsHPD=0"). The converter asks for
service with IRQ_HPD pulses, which only reach the firmware when the AP passes
them on. macOS does so on the J714s: its DCPEXT0 firmware logs
"AppleDCPDPTXController::handleIrqHpdEvent dispatching IRQ_HPD" after connect
and ~1.3 s after the first mode set. Enable dcp-hdmi.c's forwarder for
apple,t6050-dcpext too.

Tested on the J714s over three boots: requests are delivered ("HDMI:
forwarding converter service requests"), with no change to the picture or the
monitor's wake HPD cycle (see 0012).

Signed-off-by: FatBoy721 <203330788+FatBoy721@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-hdmi.c
@@ -19,7 +19,9 @@
  *    the rate those modes use, because not every request of the converter
  *    shows up as a pulse on the GPIO.
  *
- * Only the T6030 external coprocessor with a fixed HDMI route uses this.
+ * The T6030 and T6050 external coprocessors with a fixed HDMI route use this.
+ * On the T6050 J714s, macOS forwards these requests the same way: its DCP
+ * firmware logs "handleIrqHpdEvent dispatching IRQ_HPD" after the first mode set.
  */
 
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
@@ -212,7 +214,8 @@
 
 	if (!dcp->hdmi_hpd ||
 	    dcp->fixed_connector_type != DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA ||
-	    !of_device_is_compatible(dcp->dev->of_node, "apple,t6030-dcpext"))
+	    (!of_device_is_compatible(dcp->dev->of_node, "apple,t6030-dcpext") &&
+	     !of_device_is_compatible(dcp->dev->of_node, "apple,t6050-dcpext")))
 		return 0;
 
 	hdmi = devm_kzalloc(dcp->dev, sizeof(*hdmi), GFP_KERNEL);
